{# DRAFT 5 — random interruption permission
   Intent: the model does not interpret Rare/Sometimes/Often. Jinja converts the
   selected position and SkyrimNet's existing random value into allowed/blocked
   interruption classes for this call.

   PLACEHOLDERS: followerInterruption and nonFollowerInterruption are proposed
   integer settings. The percentages below are illustrative and require testing.
   This draft reuses the same `random` value as the existing silence roll, so the
   resulting correlation must also be tested.
#}
[ system ]
{% set ss = get_speaker_selector_settings() %}
{% set zerochance = ss.silenceChancePercent %}
{% set followerInterruption = default(ss.followerInterruption, 3) %}
{% set nonFollowerInterruption = default(ss.nonFollowerInterruption, 2) %}
{% set tagEngaged = ss.tagEngaged %}
{% set tagInScene = ss.tagInScene %}

{% set hasExchange = existsIn(lastSpeaker, "name") and existsIn(lastDialogueTarget, "name") %}
{% set playerSpoke = hasExchange and lastSpeaker.UUID == player.UUID %}
{% set playerWasAddressed = hasExchange and lastDialogueTarget.UUID == player.UUID %}
{% set silenceAllowed = playerWasAddressed or random < zerochance %}
{% set playerNonFollowerExchange = false %}
{% if playerSpoke and not is_follower(lastDialogueTarget.UUID) %}
{% set playerNonFollowerExchange = true %}
{% elif playerWasAddressed and not is_follower(lastSpeaker.UUID) %}
{% set playerNonFollowerExchange = true %}
{% endif %}

{% set followerMayInterrupt = false %}
{% if followerInterruption == 5 %}
{% set followerMayInterrupt = true %}
{% elif followerInterruption == 4 and random < 70 %}
{% set followerMayInterrupt = true %}
{% elif followerInterruption == 3 and random < 35 %}
{% set followerMayInterrupt = true %}
{% elif followerInterruption == 2 and random < 10 %}
{% set followerMayInterrupt = true %}
{% endif %}

{% set nonFollowerMayInterrupt = false %}
{% if nonFollowerInterruption == 4 and random < 80 %}
{% set nonFollowerMayInterrupt = true %}
{% elif nonFollowerInterruption == 3 and random < 45 %}
{% set nonFollowerMayInterrupt = true %}
{% elif nonFollowerInterruption == 2 and random < 15 %}
{% set nonFollowerMayInterrupt = true %}
{% endif %}

# Task

An NPC has spoken to a recipient. Select the next NPC reaction.

Output only {% if silenceAllowed %}`0` or {% endif %}`[exact speaker name]>[exact target]`.

The template has already decided which interruption classes are permitted on this call. Do not infer frequency from a setting label.

# Speaker permissions for this call

- The recipient may respond when that recipient is an NPC candidate.
- {{ lastSpeaker.name }} may not speak again.

{% if playerNonFollowerExchange %}
{% if followerMayInterrupt %}
- A follower other than the current participants may be selected if they have a specific, natural reaction to the completed line or recent context.
{% else %}
- Do not select a follower other than the current participants. Follower interruption is blocked on this call.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if hasExchange %}
{% if nonFollowerMayInterrupt %}
- A non-follower who is not already part of this exchange may be selected if they have a specific, natural reaction to the completed line or recent context.
{% else %}
- Do not select a non-follower who is not already part of this exchange. Non-follower interruption is blocked on this call.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

Permission does not mean that someone must speak. For every permitted candidate, consider the completed line, recent dialogue, short profile, role, and Interjection guidance together. These are evidence for a reaction, not an exhaustive checklist.

Prefer the recipient when they have the most natural immediate response. Select another permitted candidate when their reaction belongs at this moment rather than starting a new subject. Do not select anyone merely because they are nearby or because a generic line could be written for them.

{% if silenceAllowed %}
Select `0` when the player was addressed and no permitted interruption should take the floor, or when the exchange has naturally ended and no permitted candidate has an immediate reaction.
{% endif %}

Never select an NPC to comment on silence, urge the player to respond, or narrate waiting.

# Virtual NPC restrictions

- A regular NPC cannot hear or answer a Virtual NPC.
- A regular NPC cannot target a Virtual NPC.
- A Virtual NPC may target another Virtual NPC.

{{ get_scene_context(0, 0, "full") }}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
# Location

{{ location }}

# Recent Dialogue

{{ render_template("components\\event_history_compact") }}

{% if hasExchange %}
# Completed line

**{{ lastSpeaker.name }} spoke to {{ lastDialogueTarget.name }}.**
{% endif %}

# Candidates

{% for candidate in candidateDialogues %}
{% if candidate.UUID and candidate.UUID != 0 %}
{% set cinfo = decnpc(candidate.UUID) %}
{{ candidate.id }}. **{{ cinfo.name }}**{% if hasExchange and candidate.UUID == lastDialogueTarget.UUID %} **[RECIPIENT]**{% endif %}{% if hasExchange and candidate.UUID == lastSpeaker.UUID %} **[PREVIOUS SPEAKER — BLOCKED]**{% endif %}{% if not cinfo.isVirtual and is_follower(candidate.UUID) %} **[FOLLOWER]**{% endif %}{% if playerNonFollowerExchange and not cinfo.isVirtual and is_follower(candidate.UUID) and candidate.UUID != lastSpeaker.UUID and candidate.UUID != lastDialogueTarget.UUID %}{% if followerMayInterrupt %} **[INTERRUPTION PERMITTED]**{% else %} **[INTERRUPTION BLOCKED]**{% endif %}{% elif hasExchange and not cinfo.isVirtual and not is_follower(candidate.UUID) and candidate.UUID != lastSpeaker.UUID and candidate.UUID != lastDialogueTarget.UUID %}{% if nonFollowerMayInterrupt %} **[INTERRUPTION PERMITTED]**{% else %} **[INTERRUPTION BLOCKED]**{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if not cinfo.isVirtual and tagEngaged and is_in_package(candidate.UUID, "SkyrimNet_PlayerFollowPackage") %} **[ENGAGED]**{% endif %}{% if not cinfo.isVirtual and tagInScene and (is_in_faction(candidate.UUID, "SexLabAnimatingFaction") or is_in_faction(candidate.UUID, "OStimExcitementFaction")) %} **[IN SCENE]**{% endif %}{% if cinfo.isVirtual %} **[VIRTUAL NPC]**{% endif %}
   - {% if not cinfo.isVirtual %}{{ cinfo.gender }} {{ cinfo.race }}, {{ units_to_meters(candidate.distance) }}m — {% endif %}{{ render_character_profile("short_inline", candidate.UUID) }}
   - **Interjection:** {{ render_character_profile("interject_inline", candidate.UUID) }}
{% if playerNonFollowerExchange and followerMayInterrupt and not cinfo.isVirtual and is_follower(candidate.UUID) and followerInterruption >= 4 %}
   - **Personality:** {{ render_character_profile("bio_personality", candidate.UUID) }}
{% elif hasExchange and nonFollowerMayInterrupt and not cinfo.isVirtual and not is_follower(candidate.UUID) and candidate.UUID != lastSpeaker.UUID and candidate.UUID != lastDialogueTarget.UUID and nonFollowerInterruption == 4 %}
   - **Personality:** {{ render_character_profile("bio_personality", candidate.UUID) }}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

`[ENGAGED]` never overrides `[INTERRUPTION BLOCKED]`. Strongly avoid `[IN SCENE]` unless directly addressed.

# Targeting

{% if playerSpoke %}
- A responding `[RECIPIENT]` targets `player`.
{% else %}
- A responding `[RECIPIENT]` targets {{ lastSpeaker.name }}.
{% endif %}
- Another speaker targets the person they are specifically reacting to or addressing.
- Use `player` in lowercase for the player.
- Otherwise use an exact full candidate name.
- Always include a target.

Examples:

- `Aela the Huntress>Lydia`
{% if silenceAllowed %}
- `0`
{% endif %}

Do not add tags, formatting, explanation, or shortened names.

Output:
[ end user ]
